<title>GERMANY: Colonia details 1996 premium income.</title>
<headline>Colonia details 1996 premium income.</headline>
<dateline>COLOGNE, Germany 1997-03-11</dateline>
<text>
<p>Calendar 1996</p>
<p>(in millions of marks unless otherwise stated)</p>
<p>    Group gross premium income	     10,811  vs 10,148</p>
<p>Of which</p>
<p>    Non-life premiums			  5,480   vs 5,263</p>
<p>    Life premiums				4,225   vs 3,939</p>
<p>    Health premiums			    752     vs 666</p>
<p>    Indirect insurance			 345     vs 280</p>
<p>NOTE - Full name of the German insurer is CKAG Colonia Konzern AG. The insurer also said that its foreign premiums rose 17 percent to 1.3 billion marks. Around 230 million marks of the total group advance was due to the first time full consolidation of its DARAG unit and the TELLIT direct insurance unit, Colonia said.</p>
<p>--Frankfurt Newsroom, +49 69 756525</p>
</text>
